<title>UK: Shell says three more staff hurt in Nigeria.</title>
<headline>Shell says three more staff hurt in Nigeria.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Oil giant Shell said on Monday three more workers were hurt, one seriously, in an incident at an oil pumping station in Nigeria occupied at the weekend by villagers involved in a local political dispute.</p>
<p>Shell said more than 120 of its staff and contractors were still being held by the villagers who overran six oil flow stations in the western Niger Delta on Saturday.</p>
</text>
